WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.569
-My next guests have nearly

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:05.137
160 million TikTok followers
between them.

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:06.740
They host
a weekly podcast called

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.141
"Charli and Dixie: 2 Chix."

00:00:09.141 --> 00:00:11.444
And this summer, their family
will be the subject of

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:14.580
a new docu-series called
"The D'Amelio Show."

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.350
Here are
Charli and Dixie D'Amelio.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.352
Ah, look. Come on.
Look at the sisters.

00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:22.388
I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:24.757
A lot of times, we'll ask guests

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:26.226
what they've been up to
in quarantine.

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:31.531
Dixie, in your case,
you launched a music career.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.533
-Yes.
-Giant, by the way.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:37.403
You released your song
"Be Happy" in June.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:42.108
It has over
100 million YouTube views,

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:46.345
70 million streams on Spotify.

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:50.516
Wow! Did you realize it was
going to be that much of a hit?

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:55.154
-I mean, I honestly had no idea
that that would happen at all.

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:57.022
I've always wanted to do it
but never really thought

00:00:57.022 --> 00:01:01.961
it could happen,
and then it did pretty well.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:04.497
-Pretty well?
Oh, my -- Pretty well?

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:08.133
Are you kidding me?
Any plans for more music?

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:12.071
Is there an album in the works?
Anything that you can tell us?

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:13.840
-Definitely an album
at some point,

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.709
but my next song
is coming out April 9th,

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.210
which I'm very excited about.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.646
-Love it.
Alright, new jam from Dixie.

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:21.947
Alright, good.

00:01:21.947 --> 00:01:23.116
What did you think --

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.950
Because you didn't join
TikTok right away.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.485
Charli joined first.

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:28.888
What did you think when
you saw her making TikToks?

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.157
Were you like, "Cool,
I want to do that"?

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.926
-You can be honest.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:35.661
She started at a time
where TikTok was

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:37.663
still really embarrassing,

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:42.201
and I was really embarrassed
that she was posting.

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:48.241
And my friends at school were
very into what she was doing.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.342
And I was like, "Oh, my gosh.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:50.876
She is so weird,"
blah, blah, blah.

00:01:50.876 --> 00:01:51.911
-She told me.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.446
She was like,
"I just hit a 100K."

00:01:54.446 --> 00:01:55.748
And I was like,
"Oh, my goodness.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:56.782
This is so insane."

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:58.051
She was like, "Talk to me when

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:02.355
you hit a million,"
and that's when she joined.

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:05.091
-Yeah.
And then a little competition.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:09.095
But, Charli, I noticed
that you started changing up

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.763
your content
a little bit recently.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:14.200
You're posting reviews of
things like --

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.102
I don't know
what was one I just saw.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:19.839
Kinetic sand I think I saw.
-Yeah.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:22.508
-How do you know what your
followers are going to be into?

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:24.777
-If I'm going to be
honest with you,

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:27.647
it was what I was doing on
a day-to-day basis.

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:30.316
I was doing reviews
to myself in the mirror

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.651
and I was like,
"Why don't I film this?

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:34.620
This is so much fun.
Maybe people will enjoy it."

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.191
I know what people like
changes very often,

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:40.225
and I was like, "Why don't I
share this with everyone

00:02:40.225 --> 00:02:41.494
and see what they think?"

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:44.430
And I did, and people
actually really liked it.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.398
-Do you think that is the key
to being successful

00:02:46.398 --> 00:02:50.303
on social media,
just being honest?

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.671
-I think so.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:54.406
I feel like you have to be
as authentic as you can be,

00:02:54.406 --> 00:02:56.809
because people can tell
when you're not being authentic,

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:59.144
and they don't resonate
with that as much.

00:02:59.144 --> 00:03:01.514
-Before you started
doing this, Charli,

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.415
you were a competitive dancer.

00:03:03.415 --> 00:03:05.885
Would you ever go back to that?

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:10.389
-I actually just started getting
back into training.

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:16.195
We got a dance studio in my
house, which is so amazing.

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:17.663
Really never thought
that that would happen.

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:20.900
And I've been working
very closely with Blake McGrath,

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:24.570
who has kind of brought me from,
like, being out of dance

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.640
and feeling self-conscious
about myself,

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.175
because I felt
like every time I danced,

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.444
I had to, like,
prove something to everyone,

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.346
and that is not
what dance is about.

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:35.315
And he really helped me
find myself again.

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:38.284
And we are going to be
working on a solo

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.252
for this year, so hopefully
I can get back into

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:43.523
the competition scene,
because I really miss it.

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:47.626
-Well, you're on Time magazine's
TIME100 Next" list,

00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:53.132
and the person that writes about
you is Jennifer Lopez.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:57.069
What?!
Dude, you have to be happy.

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:58.538
You have to be excited.

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:00.673
That is legendary.
That is legendary.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.341
-That was insane.

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:04.577
I didn't know
she was writing about me

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:07.246
until I woke up
and I saw everyone was like,

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:08.314
"Oh, my goodness.

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:09.515
J.Lo wrote this about you."

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.585
And I was like, "Wait. Hold on.
That's not real.

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.587
That didn't happen.
I don't know what's going on."

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:17.356
That was insane to me
when I saw that.

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:20.293
What she said
really made me feel

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:23.629
so great
and so confident in myself,

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:27.533
because she made me feel like
I matter to her,

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.702
and having your idol
acknowledge you like that

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.604
is something so
amazing and something

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:34.307
I never thought
would have happened.

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:37.577
-You have your own docu-series
coming to Hulu this summer.

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.344
It's called "The D'Amelio show."

00:04:39.344 --> 00:04:44.183
I'm excited about that,
but are you -- Is it everything?

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:47.353
I mean, you are guys going to
get in fights and arguments?

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:49.756
I mean...

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.123
-We haven't yet.

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:53.559
We said,
before the filming started,

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:56.161
"Who is going to be
the first one to flip a table?

00:04:56.161 --> 00:04:57.796
That has not happened yet.
-Oh, you have to!

00:04:57.796 --> 00:04:59.965
-The tables in our house
are heavy.

00:04:59.965 --> 00:05:02.135
They're hard to flip.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:05.438
-You got to be --
Go get, like, a really --

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:07.406
like, a plastic table
or something outside

00:05:07.406 --> 00:05:08.740
and practice that.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:11.544
You have to flip a table.
-Like, a very dramatic scene.

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:14.280
-Luckily, we have not had
any of those.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.781
We don't --
-We don't really --

00:05:15.781 --> 00:05:17.683
-We don't argue
that much anymore.

00:05:17.683 --> 00:05:19.485
-Not with words.
With our eyes more.

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:22.155
-Yeah.
We're, like, literally like...

